1
00:00:36,820 --> 00:00:42,310
[She's Wild Fire]

2
00:00:43,410 --> 00:00:47,670
[Episode 22: You for the Rest of My Life]

3
00:00:47,930 --> 00:00:51,150
[Canton Fair]

4
00:00:56,280 --> 00:00:58,810
Sorry, darling.

5
00:00:58,870 --> 00:01:00,310
Hello, can we take a look?

6
00:01:00,480 --> 00:01:01,760
Yes, of course.

7
00:01:03,960 --> 00:01:06,820
This design has
such an interesting Eastern touch.

8
00:01:16,560 --> 00:01:17,560
Are you the designer?

9
00:01:17,560 --> 00:01:20,720
Yes. I'm also the founder of the brand.

10
00:01:21,520 --> 00:01:22,560
Ms. Xie,

11
00:01:24,320 --> 00:01:26,850
trying to pull one over
on our foreign guests?

12
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:28,080
Mr. Carl,

13
00:01:28,080 --> 00:01:29,320
here you are.

14
00:01:29,350 --> 00:01:30,350
I've been looking all over for you.

15
00:01:30,350 --> 00:01:31,640
Long time no see.

16
00:01:31,640 --> 00:01:32,560
Mr. Carl,

17
00:01:32,759 --> 00:01:34,860
one of the best
fashion designers in Paris.

18
00:01:34,860 --> 00:01:36,240
What is he doing at the Canton Fair?

19
00:01:36,240 --> 00:01:38,460
Didn't he stop handling
the day-to-day business a long time ago?

20
00:01:38,460 --> 00:01:39,670
Let me introduce you.

21
00:01:39,900 --> 00:01:40,660
This is

22
00:01:40,690 --> 00:01:42,479
Ms. Xie Nanfeng,

23
00:01:42,479 --> 00:01:44,360
the woman I told you about on the phone,

24
00:01:44,360 --> 00:01:46,080
the one who plagiarized the Lumina brand.

25
00:01:46,080 --> 00:01:47,340
She is the plagiarist.

26
00:01:47,560 --> 00:01:49,360
She's the one who copied Lumina?

27
00:01:56,080 --> 00:01:57,880
Everyone, take a look.

28
00:01:58,240 --> 00:02:00,000
This is Lumina's

29
00:02:00,020 --> 00:02:03,150
latest collection
from last year's Milan Fashion Week.

30
00:02:04,230 --> 00:02:05,790
Now compare it with this.

31
00:02:06,980 --> 00:02:08,340
Everyone, take a look.

32
00:02:08,370 --> 00:02:10,410
They're practically identical.

33
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:12,930
If that's not plagiarism, what is?

34
00:02:16,200 --> 00:02:17,280
Mr. Carl,

35
00:02:17,550 --> 00:02:19,180
you're a veteran in this industry.

36
00:02:19,180 --> 00:02:21,980
I know how much you hate plagiarism.

37
00:02:23,060 --> 00:02:24,340
Ms. Xie,

38
00:02:24,760 --> 00:02:29,090
looks like you've embarrassed yourself
on an international stage this time.

39
00:02:29,440 --> 00:02:30,640
Really?

40
00:02:31,390 --> 00:02:33,050
Then I definitely want to take a good look

41
00:02:33,050 --> 00:02:35,290
at what makes Lumina so great.

42
00:02:35,320 --> 00:02:37,050
Stop pretending, Xie Nanfeng.

43
00:02:37,590 --> 00:02:38,570
You think changing a few things

44
00:02:38,570 --> 00:02:40,570
makes someone else's work your own?

45
00:02:41,160 --> 00:02:43,760
Lumina is an internationally
renowned brand.

46
00:02:44,090 --> 00:02:45,710
How could a little factory like yours

47
00:02:45,710 --> 00:02:47,310
possibly compete with them?

48
00:02:47,740 --> 00:02:51,540
You're in a whole different league.

49
00:02:53,440 --> 00:02:54,480
Ms. Wan,

50
00:02:55,430 --> 00:02:59,350
I didn't realize
you admired me this much.

51
00:02:59,640 --> 00:03:00,760
What?

52
00:03:06,290 --> 00:03:10,450
The international brand
you're talking about

53
00:03:11,310 --> 00:03:12,310
is another brand

54
00:03:12,640 --> 00:03:15,440
I founded in the U.S.

55
00:03:16,250 --> 00:03:17,240
So, Ms. Xie, are you saying

56
00:03:17,240 --> 00:03:18,980
that both Lumina and Fashion Flower
are your brands?

57
00:03:18,980 --> 00:03:19,860
Yes.

58
00:03:19,960 --> 00:03:22,079
Five years ago, I went to
the U.S. to study

59
00:03:22,079 --> 00:03:25,610
at Parsons School of Design in New York,
where I founded Lumina.

60
00:03:25,810 --> 00:03:28,730
Lumina is my other brand,

61
00:03:28,860 --> 00:03:32,040
built around a fusion of
Eastern aesthetics
and modern design.

62
00:03:32,040 --> 00:03:35,130
Fashion Flower, on the other hand, is a brand
I created after returning to Shencheng.

63
00:03:35,130 --> 00:03:37,560
I wanted to create a brand

64
00:03:37,579 --> 00:03:39,780
that truly belongs to Chinese women.

65
00:03:40,630 --> 00:03:42,520
The two brands share the same roots,

66
00:03:42,520 --> 00:03:43,620
yet they are completely different.

67
00:03:43,620 --> 00:03:44,860
And yet today,

68
00:03:44,990 --> 00:03:47,390
someone has taken one of my own creations

69
00:03:47,420 --> 00:03:51,079
and used it to accuse me, its creator,
of plagiarizing my own work.

70
00:03:52,040 --> 00:03:53,690
Don't you find that ridiculous?

71
00:03:53,690 --> 00:03:56,240
Ms. Wan, it seems your accusations
against Ms. Xie aren't true.

72
00:03:56,240 --> 00:03:56,720
Nonsense.

73
00:03:56,720 --> 00:03:57,360
It's fake.

74
00:03:57,360 --> 00:03:58,840
-Ms. Wan, did you resort to these dirty tricks
-It's fake.

75
00:03:58,840 --> 00:03:59,600
because Dongmen Clothing Trade Center

76
00:03:59,600 --> 00:04:00,680
took away your business?

77
00:04:00,680 --> 00:04:02,080
It's all fake.

78
00:04:02,930 --> 00:04:04,170
Mr. Carl,

79
00:04:04,200 --> 00:04:05,320
I was misled.

80
00:04:05,390 --> 00:04:07,070
I only said what I was told.

81
00:04:07,320 --> 00:04:08,240
Is that so?

82
00:04:10,790 --> 00:04:13,680
You told him there was a designer here
who was plagiarizing

83
00:04:13,680 --> 00:04:15,710
and tarnishing the industry's reputation,

84
00:04:15,710 --> 00:04:18,120
and you asked him to
come and judge the matter.

85
00:04:18,120 --> 00:04:19,720
He does hate plagiarism.

86
00:04:20,279 --> 00:04:21,339
But he hates people

87
00:04:21,680 --> 00:04:23,360
who use underhanded schemes

88
00:04:23,720 --> 00:04:26,250
to frame others and
bring them down even more.

89
00:04:27,050 --> 00:04:28,010
It's unethical,

90
00:04:30,980 --> 00:04:33,110
and he despises that kind of behavior.

91
00:04:34,500 --> 00:04:35,659
That's all.

92
00:04:36,600 --> 00:04:37,790
It's all right, Mr. Carl.

93
00:04:37,790 --> 00:04:39,320
I'm willing to forgive her.

94
00:04:42,380 --> 00:04:44,380
You called Lumina today

95
00:04:44,640 --> 00:04:45,640
asking for proof.

96
00:04:46,159 --> 00:04:47,800
I was the one who answered.

97
00:04:49,240 --> 00:04:49,880
You!

98
00:04:59,440 --> 00:05:00,160
Miss Xie,

99
00:05:00,640 --> 00:05:02,600
would you be interested
in finding somewhere quiet

100
00:05:02,600 --> 00:05:03,670
to talk about your designs?

101
00:05:03,670 --> 00:05:04,720
Yes, my pleasure.

102
00:05:04,720 --> 00:05:05,440
Please.

103
00:05:15,340 --> 00:05:17,470
Mr. Carl thinks you're very talented.

104
00:05:18,920 --> 00:05:21,120
He says you're a young designer to watch

105
00:05:23,240 --> 00:05:25,300
and that you have a very clear vision.

106
00:05:26,400 --> 00:05:28,060
You're really thinking about

107
00:05:29,920 --> 00:05:31,880
how to bring the qipao
back into everyday life.

108
00:05:31,880 --> 00:05:33,080
Thank you, Mr. Carl.

109
00:05:33,880 --> 00:05:35,810
Tradition needs to be passed down,

110
00:05:35,960 --> 00:05:39,220
but more importantly,
it needs to keep pace with the times.

111
00:05:43,320 --> 00:05:44,560
Mr. Carl has read some articles

112
00:05:44,560 --> 00:05:46,290
about your Lumina collection.

113
00:05:47,120 --> 00:05:50,400
It has a good reputation
in certain circles in Europe and America.

114
00:05:50,400 --> 00:05:51,860
But have you ever wondered

115
00:05:52,070 --> 00:05:52,830
why it hasn't

116
00:05:53,400 --> 00:05:55,280
made a bigger splash?

117
00:05:55,880 --> 00:05:57,120
I have, actually.

118
00:05:58,000 --> 00:06:00,730
I think there may still be
a layer between the two.

119
00:06:01,320 --> 00:06:03,560
I'm telling an Eastern story

120
00:06:03,560 --> 00:06:05,160
through a Western lens.

121
00:06:05,520 --> 00:06:06,880
It's certainly innovative,

122
00:06:06,880 --> 00:06:07,640
but

123
00:06:09,080 --> 00:06:11,360
perhaps it lacks the depth and resonance

124
00:06:11,360 --> 00:06:13,480
that come from its roots.

125
00:06:19,240 --> 00:06:21,370
So now you're back to designing qipaos

126
00:06:22,050 --> 00:06:23,530
to find those roots?

127
00:06:23,560 --> 00:06:24,240
Yes.

128
00:06:24,640 --> 00:06:28,680
And I want the world to see

129
00:06:28,960 --> 00:06:30,960
the true beauty of Chinese women,

130
00:06:30,960 --> 00:06:33,950
rather than reducing the East

131
00:06:33,980 --> 00:06:35,040
to exotic symbols.

132
00:06:38,520 --> 00:06:40,560
Give her the invitation.

133
00:06:42,290 --> 00:06:44,030
This year's Paris Fashion Week committee

134
00:06:44,030 --> 00:06:45,750
has given Mr. Carl

135
00:06:45,790 --> 00:06:47,830
a spot for an emerging Asian designer.

136
00:06:47,830 --> 00:06:49,490
He's been searching for the right candidate
for quite some time,

137
00:06:49,490 --> 00:06:51,090
but hasn't found anyone suitable.

138
00:06:51,090 --> 00:06:52,890
Then he saw your qipao designs.

139
00:06:52,909 --> 00:06:54,710
He believes your idea

140
00:06:54,790 --> 00:06:57,190
of combining traditional craftsmanship

141
00:06:57,510 --> 00:06:58,510
with modern technology

142
00:06:58,510 --> 00:07:00,170
could find its stage in Paris.

143
00:07:01,830 --> 00:07:03,270
Thank you, Mr. Carl.

144
00:07:04,230 --> 00:07:06,990
I'd absolutely love to

145
00:07:06,990 --> 00:07:09,790
go to Paris with you
and bring the qipao with me.

146
00:07:15,150 --> 00:07:17,930
[Six months later, Shencheng]

147
00:07:22,920 --> 00:07:23,600
Mr. Chu,

148
00:07:23,630 --> 00:07:25,910
do you have money to burn?

149
00:07:28,070 --> 00:07:28,950
What's wrong?

150
00:07:29,410 --> 00:07:31,010
These are all my treasures!

151
00:07:32,090 --> 00:07:33,810
When Nannan grows up,

152
00:07:33,850 --> 00:07:35,250
I want to show them to him.

153
00:07:35,310 --> 00:07:36,510
And if we ever

154
00:07:36,530 --> 00:07:39,570
have grandchildren,

155
00:07:39,600 --> 00:07:41,760
I'll show them to them, too.

156
00:07:42,430 --> 00:07:44,110
They need to know

157
00:07:44,110 --> 00:07:45,570
how amazing their mother,

158
00:07:45,810 --> 00:07:48,030
grandmother, and great-grandmother were.

159
00:07:48,030 --> 00:07:49,710
Grandchildren?

160
00:07:50,340 --> 00:07:51,740
How many do you want?

161
00:07:52,030 --> 00:07:53,790
You're really thinking that far ahead.

162
00:07:53,790 --> 00:07:54,590
I don't care.

163
00:07:54,590 --> 00:07:55,670
No one

164
00:07:55,670 --> 00:07:56,650
touches my things.

165
00:07:56,650 --> 00:07:58,380
They're our family heirlooms.

166
00:08:03,950 --> 00:08:04,790
Nanfeng,

167
00:08:06,040 --> 00:08:07,440
you're truly amazing.

168
00:08:07,930 --> 00:08:09,410
Of course.

169
00:08:10,270 --> 00:08:12,910
But Paris deserves some credit, too.

170
00:08:13,450 --> 00:08:16,720
Our overseas orders have been pouring in,

171
00:08:16,810 --> 00:08:18,730
and the production lines
can barely keep up.

172
00:08:18,730 --> 00:08:21,770
Then we need to find a reliable
logistics company.

173
00:08:21,800 --> 00:08:23,670
With orders coming in at this volume,

174
00:08:23,670 --> 00:08:24,870
we have to be careful.

175
00:08:26,210 --> 00:08:27,660
I've contacted

176
00:08:27,690 --> 00:08:29,570
Xunda International Logistics.

177
00:08:29,840 --> 00:08:32,669
They have networks in Shencheng,
Hong Kong, and overseas,

178
00:08:32,669 --> 00:08:34,070
and they have an excellent reputation.

179
00:08:34,070 --> 00:08:36,000
We signed the contract a while ago.

180
00:08:36,750 --> 00:08:38,110
That's good.

181
00:08:38,380 --> 00:08:40,179
Now, my favorite female tycoon,

182
00:08:41,309 --> 00:08:46,310
shouldn't we go inside and get some rest?

183
00:08:53,050 --> 00:08:54,850
Ms. Wan, don't worry.

184
00:08:55,240 --> 00:08:57,950
The first shipment of Xie Nanfeng's goods
going by sea to Europe

185
00:08:57,950 --> 00:09:00,210
will all be in our warehouse by tomorrow.

186
00:09:00,750 --> 00:09:02,670
Good, very good.

187
00:09:04,730 --> 00:09:08,120
That woman, Xie Nanfeng,
thinks one trip to Paris
makes her untouchable.

188
00:09:08,120 --> 00:09:10,050
As soon as her shipment arrives tomorrow,

189
00:09:10,050 --> 00:09:12,330
I'll switch it out on her.

190
00:09:13,390 --> 00:09:14,110
We'll take

191
00:09:14,310 --> 00:09:15,440
the whole shipment.

192
00:09:15,550 --> 00:09:16,550
You get rid of

193
00:09:16,630 --> 00:09:17,910
the real goods

194
00:09:18,270 --> 00:09:21,550
and replace them with junk.
Then send
the junk to her customers in Europe.

195
00:09:21,550 --> 00:09:23,310
Just imagine the fallout.

196
00:09:23,850 --> 00:09:25,270
Her reputation will be ruined,

197
00:09:25,270 --> 00:09:26,910
and she'll be hit
with massive compensation claims.

198
00:09:26,910 --> 00:09:28,310
This is a brilliant move.

199
00:09:28,950 --> 00:09:30,790
No one will ever know.

200
00:09:31,150 --> 00:09:32,630
By the time she finds out,

201
00:09:32,630 --> 00:09:34,890
it'll be too late to do anything about it.

202
00:09:35,330 --> 00:09:36,850
Tell our guys

203
00:09:37,010 --> 00:09:39,250
to stay sharp these next few days.

204
00:09:39,590 --> 00:09:40,390
Keep a close eye on her,

205
00:09:40,390 --> 00:09:41,530
and keep a close eye on the shipment.

206
00:09:41,530 --> 00:09:42,250
Got it?

207
00:09:46,060 --> 00:09:47,060
This time,

208
00:09:47,410 --> 00:09:51,010
I'm going to make sure
you never get back on your feet.
